Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:36:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: start each spatial audio update from a silent
 buffer

The static objects are added into the render buffer GetBuffer returns,
and that buffer holds whatever the driver left in it: a driver that
hands back the same area each period (the iOS one does, as Windows
allows) had every period added onto the last. DRAGON QUEST VII
Reimagined Demo (2499870) renders through a 7.1.4 static bed, and the
phone played loud noise that grew to five times full scale within
twenty seconds.

Class: fix
Evidence: docs/decisions/0199-spatial-audio-starts-each-update-silent.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/mmdevapi/spatialaudio.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/spatialaudio.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/spatialaudio.c
index 864b33136e6..e348b9d6252 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/spatialaudio.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/spatialaudio.c
@@ -417,6 +417,10 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI SAORS_BeginUpdatingAudioObjects(ISpatialAudioObjectRenderS
             return hr;
         }
 
+        /* The static objects are added into this buffer, and GetBuffer hands it
+         * over with whatever it held before: start it silent. */
+        memset(This->buf, 0, This->update_frames * This->stream_fmtex.Format.nBlockAlign);
+
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(object, &This->objects, SpatialAudioObjectImpl, entry){
             memset(object->buf, 0, This->update_frames * This->sa_client->object_fmtex.Format.nBlockAlign);
         }
